{
  "_about": "Canada's 47 national parks and national park reserves and Rouge National Urban Park, as Parks Canada lists them (parks.canada.ca/pn-np, checked 18 November 2026; the page lists exactly these 48). IDs are permanent: user logs point at them. 'name' is the park's short English name, the official name without its designation, which is 'designation'; 'officialName' is the English name Parks Canada titles its page with, and the French 'localNames' entry the name its French page (parcs.canada.ca/pn-np) uses. An Indigenous name is given only where Parks Canada uses one beside the park's name: 'Tongait KakKasuangita SilakKijapvinga' (Inuttitut) on Torngat Mountains' page and 'Nahʔą Dehé' (Dehcho Dene) on Nahanni's; names that are already Indigenous (Auyuittuq, Gwaii Haanas, Thaidene Nëné) are the name. 'cpcadParentId' keys the park to the Canadian Protected and Conserved Areas Database (CPCAD, PARENT_ID, Parks Canada Agency as provider): every CPCAD record with that parent and a park designation is one piece of the outline (Kejimkujik's inland park and Seaside, Wood Buffalo's Alberta and Northwest Territories parts, the marine parts of coastal parks), and the program-support lands Gulf Islands also lists are not. 'passportRegion' is Unigrids' own grouping (ADR 0014) by the park's province or territory; Wood Buffalo, mostly in Alberta, is filed with the North. 'pcPage' is the park's page on parks.canada.ca, from which its brochures and maps are read. 'attendancePlace' is the park's row in Parks Canada's attendance table (open.canada.ca, 'Parks Canada attendance 2025_26'): Mount Revelstoke and Glacier are counted together there and carry no figure; Gwaii Haanas's row counts the park reserve, the marine conservation area reserve and the heritage site together; Rouge, Torngat Mountains, Akami-Uapishkᵁ-KakKasuak-Mealy Mountains, Vuntut, Thaidene Nëné, Qausuittuq and Ukkusiksalik have no row. 'reachedBy' is how a park with no road to it is reached, paraphrased from its 'Plan your visit' and 'How to get here' pages. Parks Canada also lists Pituamkek National Park Reserve (Prince Edward Island) in CPCAD as an interim reserve; it is not on the national parks page and not here. Founding years and areas are curated in each guide's facts.",
